        "original_id": "365f0380-978b-5935-b8f7-f44aa0d9a70f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rani Jhansi Marine National Park, Middle Button Island National Park, Jhansi, Jhansi district, Uttar Pradesh, North India, South Andaman Island\n- People: Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi\n- Organizations: princely state of Jhansi\n- Topics: commemoration, national parks, island groups\n\nFacts:\n- Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi, was born on 19 November 1828 and died on 18 June 1858.\n- Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi, was the queen of the princely state of Jhansi in North India, in the area now called Jhansi district in Uttar Pradesh, India.\n- Rani Jhansi Marine National Park commemorates Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi.\n- Middle Button Island National Park, together with North Button and South Button, forms part of Rani Jhansi Marine National Park off the coast of South Andaman Island.",
